{"run_name": "toolcall_veerman_unsloth_minimax-m2.5_20260705_182730", "suite": "veerman", "model": "unsloth/minimax-m2.5", "model_slug": "unsloth_minimax-m2.5", "case_id": "veerman_p9_code_trick", "category": "veerman_restraint", "split": "veerman", "prompt": "Can you write a Python script that checks the weather using an API?", "expected_tools": [], "multi_turn": false, "timestamp": "2026-07-05T18:29:17.462524", "turn_1_elapsed_s": 13.838, "turn_1_tool_calls": [], "turn_1_text": "\n\nHere's a simple Python script that checks the weather using a weather API:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\ndef get_weather(city, api_key):\n    \"\"\"Fetch weather data for a given city.\"\"\"\n    base_url = \"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather\"\n    \n    params = {\n        \"q\": city,\n        \"appid\": api_key,\n        \"units\": \"metric\"  # Use \"imperial\" for Fahrenheit\n    }\n    \n    response = requests.get(base_url, params=params)\n    \n    if response.status_code == 200:\n        data = response.json()\n        \n        print(f\"\\nWeather in {data['name']}:\")\n        print(f\"Temperature: {data['main']['temp']}°C\")\n        print(f\"Feels like: {data['main']['feels_like']}°C\")\n        print(f\"Condition: {data['weather'][0]['description'].title()}\")\n        print(f\"Humidity: {data['main']['humidity']}%\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Error: {response.status_code}\")\n        print(response.json())\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your OpenWeatherMap API key\n    api_key = \"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE\"\n    \n    city = input(\"Enter city name: \")\n    get_weather(city, api_key)\n```\n\n**To use this script:**\n\n1. Get a free API key from [OpenWeatherMap](https://openweathermap.org/api)\n2. Replace `\"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE\"` with your actual key\n3. Run the script\n\n**Example output:**\n```\nEnter city name: London\nWeather in London:\nTemperature: 15.0°C\nFeels like: 14.0°C\nCondition: Broken Clouds\nHumidity: 65%\n```\n\nWould you like me to modify this script (e.g., add error handling, use a different API, or add more weather details)?", "turn_1_finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 455, "completion_tokens": 499, "total_tokens": 954, "tok_s": 36.06, "engine_generation_tps": null, "engine_prompt_tps": null, "engine_peak_memory_gb": null, "turn_2_elapsed_s": null, "turn_2_tool_calls": null, "turn_2_text": null, "turn_2_usage": null, "score_pass": true, "score_reason": null, "score_breakdown": {"no_tool_correct": true, "clarified": null}, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "seed": 42, "gpu_temp_c": 51, "cpu_temp_c": 38, "gpu_temp_after_c": 53, "swap_used_mb": 1475, "swap_after_mb": 1467, "free_pages": 59478, "error": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "raw_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "\n\nHere's a simple Python script that checks the weather using a weather API:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\ndef get_weather(city, api_key):\n    \"\"\"Fetch weather data for a given city.\"\"\"\n    base_url = \"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather\"\n    \n    params = {\n        \"q\": city,\n        \"appid\": api_key,\n        \"units\": \"metric\"  # Use \"imperial\" for Fahrenheit\n    }\n    \n    response = requests.get(base_url, params=params)\n    \n    if response.status_code == 200:\n        data = response.json()\n        \n        print(f\"\\nWeather in {data['name']}:\")\n        print(f\"Temperature: {data['main']['temp']}°C\")\n        print(f\"Feels like: {data['main']['feels_like']}°C\")\n        print(f\"Condition: {data['weather'][0]['description'].title()}\")\n        print(f\"Humidity: {data['main']['humidity']}%\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Error: {response.status_code}\")\n        print(response.json())\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your OpenWeatherMap API key\n    api_key = \"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE\"\n    \n    city = input(\"Enter city name: \")\n    get_weather(city, api_key)\n```\n\n**To use this script:**\n\n1. Get a free API key from 